<h2>Mediaocean</h2>
<p>Mediaocean is a large enterprise media management platform used for campaign workflow, Prisma digital buying, finance, and operational media processes.</p>
<p><strong>Best for:</strong> Large agencies and holding company teams standardizing media operations across many clients.</p>
<p><strong>Pricing:</strong> Enterprise custom quote.</p>
<p><strong>Key differentiators vs Strata:</strong> Broader enterprise footprint across Prisma and media finance workflows; evaluation often comes down to installed base, integrations, and agency process fit.</p>
<p><a href="/mediaocean">Learn more about Mediaocean on MPT -></a></p>

<h2>Advantage</h2>
<p>Advantage is an agency management and finance platform that supports billing, accounting, media operations, project management, and reporting.</p>
<p><strong>Best for:</strong> Agencies where finance, job costing, and operational accounting are central to the media workflow.</p>
<p><strong>Pricing:</strong> Enterprise custom quote.</p>
<p><strong>Key differentiators vs Strata:</strong> Stronger agency management and finance orientation; Strata is more directly associated with media buying workflows.</p>
<p><a href="/advantage">Learn more about Advantage on MPT -></a></p>

<h2>BluHorn</h2>
<p>BluHorn focuses on media planning and buying workflows, especially for broadcast TV, cable, radio, and local media teams.</p>
<p><strong>Best for:</strong> Independent agencies that need practical buying workflow without a full enterprise media operations rollout.</p>
<p><strong>Pricing:</strong> Mid-market subscription; confirm current rates with BluHorn.</p>
<p><strong>Key differentiators vs Strata:</strong> Lighter adoption path and narrower operational footprint.</p>
<p><a href="/bluhorn">Learn more about BluHorn on MPT -></a></p>

<h2>Bionic</h2>
<p>Bionic provides media planning, flowcharts, RFPs, buying workflow, and campaign management for agencies.</p>
<p><strong>Best for:</strong> Agencies that want structured planning and buying workflow without heavy enterprise implementation.</p>
<p><strong>Pricing:</strong> Mid-market to custom, depending on seats and modules.</p>
<p><strong>Key differentiators vs Strata:</strong> More planner-friendly and workflow-focused; Strata is stronger where billing and reconciliation are central.</p>
<p><a href="/bionic">Learn more about Bionic on MPT -></a></p>

<h2>AdLib Planner</h2>
<p>AdLib Planner is a media planning system used for plan building, campaign structure, and planning workflow.</p>
<p><strong>Best for:</strong> Teams that need a planning-centric alternative and do not require Strata-scale finance operations.</p>
<p><strong>Pricing:</strong> Custom quote.</p>
<p><strong>Key differentiators vs Strata:</strong> More focused on plan construction and workflow than full operational media buying infrastructure.</p>

<h2>How to Choose</h2>
<p>Start with the operational job you need the system to do. If finance, billing, vendor reconciliation, and agency-wide governance are the priority, compare Strata with Mediaocean and Advantage. If the main need is planning, buying workflow, and easier adoption, evaluate BluHorn, Bionic, and AdLib Planner.</p>

<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<h3>What is the closest Strata alternative?</h3>
<p>Mediaocean is usually the closest enterprise alternative because both support large-scale media operations and agency workflow.</p>
<h3>Which Strata alternative is best for smaller agencies?</h3>
<p>BluHorn and Bionic are often better fits for smaller agencies because they are more focused and generally easier to evaluate.</p>
<h3>Do Strata alternatives publish pricing?</h3>
<p>Some mid-market tools provide more pricing guidance, but enterprise systems such as Mediaocean and Advantage are usually custom-quoted.</p>
<h3>Should finance own the evaluation?</h3>
<p>Finance should be involved if the system will touch billing, invoicing, reconciliation, accounting codes, or client profitability reporting.</p>
<h3>Is Strata replaceable with spreadsheets?</h3>
<p>Only for lightweight planning. Once buying, approvals, billing, and reconciliation are operationally important, a structured platform is usually required.</p>

